id: fortnite
name: Fortnite (survival play)
games: Fortnite, Fortnite Battle Royale, فورت نايت
---
Fortnite mobile, played with touches only. The controls are the user's own layout: LOOK at the screenshot to find them. Usually a movement stick at the bottom-left, a look area on the right half (drag to turn), a big fire button on the right, jump and crouch near it, a pickup button that shows near the middle-right when you stand on loot, and the inventory along the top or right. The phone also reads the words on the screen for you (list with positions): press a button with {"t":"text","text":"READY"} instead of guessing a cell. Continue, Play again, Skip, Ready and similar are pressed by the phone itself before you are asked.
LOBBY: if a news, rewards or update popup covers the lobby, close it (its X, or Close, or back). Tap PLAY, check the mode the user asked for (default: the one selected; Zero Build is gentler), then Ready/Start. While it says searching or loading, reply {"act":"wait"} and nothing else. Never open the Item Shop, V-Bucks, Battle Pass, gifts, offers, or anything with a price.
BUS AND LANDING: on the bus screen tap the jump button once the bus is past the middle of the map. Pick a spot away from the bus path and from the crowd: the edge of the map or a small house, not the big named towns where everyone lands. Push the stick forward and drag the look area downward to dive, open the glider when its button shows, keep the stick forward and glide to a roof. A landing that is far from everyone is a good landing.
LOOT FIRST, THEN THE CIRCLE: walk into houses (the door is usually open), look for glowing chests and floor items, tap pickup while it shows. Priority: a weapon, then shield and healing, then ammo and materials. Check the inventory once after a pickup so you know what you hold. Heal (hold the heal item) when health is low and nobody is near. Do not stand still: a stationary player is the easiest to hit.
STORM: the storm is purple. The phone tells you when much of the screen is purple. Then stop looting and run toward the middle of the white circle on the mini-map; keep the stick forward, drag the look area to turn toward it. If the circle is far, run first and loot on the way. The circle shrinks several times, so move earlier than feels needed and finish inside it, behind a building or a hill.
OTHER PLAYERS: this skill plays to survive, loot and reach the end circle, not to fight. If someone is near, break line of sight (go behind a wall or a hill), keep moving away, and avoid open ground. It does NOT aim at or shoot other players for the user: automated aiming is cheating, breaks Epic's rules and can get the user's account banned. If the user wants a fight, tell him in one line to take over the controls.
STUCK: if the screen did not change after a move you are against a wall or a fence. Sidestep, jump (the phone does this by itself when roaming), then turn the camera and try another way. Water: swim across or go around, do not stand in it.
DEAD OR WON: after elimination use Leave or Return to Lobby (not Spectate), then queue again if time remains. Say in one short line what happened and how it went (where you landed, how long you lasted).
FAST POLICIES that work here: spam the pickup button while it is visible, only after you saw where it is on THIS phone: {"policy":{"ms":5000,"hz":3,"rules":[{"when":{"blob":{"color":"#ffffff","region":[0.6,0.45,0.95,0.75],"pick":"largest","min":0.004}},"do":[{"tapblob":[0,0]}],"cool":500}]}}
LAYOUT AND ROAM: on your first look at the match HUD return "layout" with stick, look, jump and pickup positions (fractions of the screen). After that, while you are just moving and looting, reply state playing with an empty do: the phone walks forward, sweeps the camera, jumps and taps pickup for about six seconds by itself using the saved layout (fast, no waiting for you), then you look again and decide: loot found, storm warning, someone near (move away), dead (leave to lobby). Keep each look short.
